<section class="document-page">
<h1>Deposit product agreement</h1><p class="sandbox-label"><strong>Sandbox specimen</strong> · Fictional institution and customer data.</p><p class="document-reference">${facts.documentReference} · ${facts.issuedOn}</p>
<dl class="key-details"><div><dt>Applicant</dt><dd>${facts.partyName}</dd></div><div><dt>Product</dt><dd>${facts.productName}</dd></div><div><dt>Product revision</dt><dd>${facts.productVersion}</dd></div><div><dt>Account</dt><dd>${facts.accountNumber}</dd></div><div><dt>Contract</dt><dd>${facts.contractReference}</dd></div><div><dt>Proposed effective date</dt><dd>${facts.effectiveDate}</dd></div><div><dt>Currency</dt><dd>${facts.currency}</dd></div><div><dt>Execution status</dt><dd>Unsigned sandbox draft</dd></div></dl><h2>1. Purpose and account ownership</h2><p>This demonstration agreement describes a current account held by ${facts.partyName}, customer reference ${facts.partyReference}, under product ${facts.productCode}. The separately retained account-holder association establishes who may own or operate the account. Opening, identity checks and activation are business operations; this reading copy does not complete them.</p><h2>2. Services and instructions</h2><p>The illustrated account supports permitted deposits, withdrawals and payment instructions through configured channels. Each instruction remains subject to current authority, account controls, available funds and the supported payment service. Submission is distinct from execution, clearing and settlement. A pending instruction must be recovered using its original reference.</p>
<div class="document-legal-note"><strong>Demonstration document.</strong> Firefly Sandbox Financial Services is a fictional demonstration entity. This is an unsigned sandbox specimen with fictional data, not an approved customer form, legal certification, audited report, signature or payment evidence. Approved institution details, source facts, product terms and jurisdiction wording require their own governed revision and authorization.</div>
</section>
<section class="document-page">
<h2>Pricing, statements, and account controls</h2><p class="sandbox-label"><strong>Sandbox specimen</strong> · Fictional institution and customer data.</p><p class="document-reference">${facts.documentReference} · ${facts.issuedOn}</p>
<h2>3. Pricing schedule</h2><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Illustrated term</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Monthly account fee</td><td class="amount">${facts.monthlyFee?number?string["#,##0.00"]} ${facts.currency}</td></tr><tr><td>Month-end booked balance for waiver</td><td class="amount">${facts.feeWaiverBalance?number?string["#,##0.00"]} ${facts.currency}</td></tr><tr><td>Authorized overdraft in this product variant</td><td class="amount">${facts.overdraftLimit?number?string["#,##0.00"]} ${facts.currency}</td></tr><tr><td>Credit interest rate</td><td>${facts.creditInterestRate}</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The example monthly fee is waived when the authoritative month-end booked balance meets the stated threshold. Assessment, calendar, posting, reversal and disclosure belong to the versioned pricing workflow ${facts.pricingReference}. Other products may provide an approved credit facility with separate terms and enforcement.</p><p>These proposed prices apply only after the actual agreement is executed and its approved effective conditions are met. This unsigned draft does not reprice historical charges, which retain their own assessment and policy references.</p>
<h2>4. Statements and balances</h2><p>Statements identify their period, booked movements and opening/closing balances. Reserved money is distinct from booked money; available funds also depend on controls and any approved facility. Historical certificates identify their own cutoff and source snapshot. Report an unexpected entry through ${facts.serviceReference}; the configured complaint workflow records the request and its outcome.</p><h2>5. Changes, controls and ending the relationship</h2><p>A new governed revision records approved changes to product or pricing terms. Account restrictions and their release require current authority. Closing requires the supported closure workflow, settlement of obligations, treatment of pending items and retained final evidence. Deleting a record or generating a closure letter does not close an account.</p>
<div class="document-legal-note"><strong>Demonstration document.</strong> Firefly Sandbox Financial Services is a fictional demonstration entity. This is an unsigned sandbox specimen with fictional data, not an approved customer form, legal certification, audited report, signature or payment evidence. Approved institution details, source facts, product terms and jurisdiction wording require their own governed revision and authorization.</div>
</section>
